{"id":"chatcmpl-e764f94c-590c-4ac8-8ab9-996a49645a16","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248786,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question about a medical finding by combining two independent visual verification methods: an expert visual QA tool and a grounded detection/report tool. The key insight is that laterality must be interpreted relative to anatomical orientation markers (e.g., L marker), not raw image coordinates. Cross-checking two independent tools and reconciling their outputs against orientation context yields a confident answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on left/right laterality, always anchor interpretation to the image's anatomical orientation marker rather than raw pixel position.\",\n    \"Use two independent verification tools (e.g., expert QA + grounded detection) and require their conclusions to agree before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"For presence-and-location questions, first confirm the finding exists, then separately resolve its side/location to avoid conflating the two judgments.\",\n    \"Prefer tools that return grounded coordinates or structured reports over free-text-only tools, since coordinates enable independent laterality checks.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Confirm finding presence first, then resolve laterality using orientation markers; cross-validate with a second tool that returns coordinates.\",\n    \"Binary visual classification\": \"Treat each option as a hypothesis to verify independently rather than picking the most plausible; require converging evidence.\",\n    \"Tool-augmented reasoning\": \"Chain a descriptive/QA tool with a grounded-detection tool so one provides semantics and the other provides spatial verification.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Verify the anatomical orientation marker (e.g., L/R) is identified before interpreting any left/right finding.\",\n    \"Confirm both independent tools agree on presence and laterality before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":441,"total_tokens":802,"completion_tokens":361,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":441},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":361}}}